{"ts": "2026-04-19T00:05:00Z", "event": "clarify_critic", "feature": "shot-fixture-regression-harness", "findings": ["Intent clarity rated HIGH but the ticket never states the success condition as 'pytest passes on clean checkout / fails on drift'; tolerance semantics (what counts as 'categorical' vs 'float', how timestamps/nested structures are handled) are not defined; platform-determinism for 1e-6 float comparison not addressed.", "Intent conflates two purposes: regression harness (byte-stable goldens) vs fixture library (representative diversity); success criteria for each differ.", "Scope rated HIGH but candidates (b) and (c) are open-ended: 'pick any pre-bloom-era shot; if none exists, capture one via hardware'; 'grep history for weight_anomalies; substitute if none exist'. Only (a) Shot 170 is pinned.", "Scope claim 'explicitly excludes CI creation' misreads the source — 'Test is wired into any existing CI config; if none exists, note that in the epic and flag as a follow-up' is a conditional inclusion with branching work, not an exclusion.", "Refresh mechanism forks between a new gaggimate_mcp.tools.refresh_fixtures module and README step-by-step instructions; assessment treated as bounded deliverable.", "Requirements alignment 'skipped — no requirements/ directory' ignores that sibling tickets 015/018/021 and epic 013 function as de facto requirements via the Blocks relationship; golden JSON schema must be compatible with what those tickets will modify.", "Complexity 'complex' rating uses the blocking-other-tickets argument as evidence, which is actually criticality reasoning; ignores a real complexity source — transformer output determinism under 1e-6 tolerance is an implicit sub-scope.", "Criticality 'high' leans on the 'shared skills / workflow infrastructure' phrase but a pytest fixture directory in mcp/tests/ is not skills/lifecycle/hooks/workflow; impact is recoverable and affects timing of downstream tickets, not severity.", "Source frontmatter shows status: in_progress and lifecycle_phase: research already set; assessment drew no inference from possible pre-work or status drift."], "dispositions": {"apply": 4, "dismiss": 4, "ask": 1}, "applied_fixes": ["Revised scope-boundedness reasoning: CI wiring is conditional inclusion (verified: no .github/workflows/ exists, so this resolves to flag-as-follow-up per the acceptance criterion) — not an exclusion.", "Revised requirements-alignment note: sibling tickets 015/018/021 serve as de facto requirements via Blocks relationship; research must verify golden JSON schema (TransformedSample + ShotSummary) compatibility with planned modifications in 015 (weight-flow surfacing) and 018 (DDSA port).", "Revised complexity reasoning: dropped the blocking-relationship argument (that was criticality reasoning); kept 'complex' tier on the grounds of 8+ files on minimum path, new regression-fixture pattern, and potential transformer-determinism sub-scope. Added open research question about determinism.", "Revised criticality from high to medium: test infrastructure in mcp/tests/ is not shared skill/lifecycle/hook/workflow; impact is recoverable (broken fixture delays downstream tickets but does not corrupt data or break shipping features)."], "dismissals": [{"finding_index": 0, "rationale": "Intent-level goal is clear (regression harness + goldens + pytest + README + refresh procedure). Tolerance semantics and platform determinism are Spec-level implementation details, not intent gaps; added to Open Questions for Research."}, {"finding_index": 1, "rationale": "The two purposes are complementary, not conflicting: representative fixtures serve both the library's documentation goal and the harness's drift-catching goal. The three archetypes (bloom-slide / decline / BT-artifact) are the common denominator."}, {"finding_index": 4, "rationale": "Self-resolved by checking mcp/src/gaggimate_mcp/tools/ — the namespace exists, so refresh_fixtures would fit existing conventions. The OR clause in the ticket is an acceptable implementer-choice escape valve: if the procedure is short, skip the script. Added to Open Questions for Research to let spec pick."}, {"finding_index": 8, "rationale": "Status and lifecycle_phase fields were populated by the /lifecycle bootstrap ~10 minutes before this Clarify phase — not pre-work drift. Frontmatter reflects the in-progress lifecycle, not prior implementation effort."}], "status": "ok"}
